THIRD-PARTY DATA ATTRIBUTION

The package's own code is MIT-licensed (see LICENSE). Some dataset fields
are adapted from third-party sources under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International (CC-BY-4.0). This file satisfies the CC-BY-4.0 attribution
requirement (credit + license link + adaptation note, in a reasonable
manner). Per-field provenance, including retrieval dates, lives in
data/SOURCES.md.

1. Nepal Administrative Divisions (open-admin-data)
   Source:  https://github.com/open-admin-data/nepal-administrative-divisions
   License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0),
            https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   Used for: geographic coordinates (latitude/longitude) at province, district
            and local-unit level; Devanagari names (as the second bilingual
            source, and as a fallback where abinrimal's roster is short in a
            district or blank for a row); and Nepal Post postal codes at
            local-unit level.
   Adaptation: values are merged with other sources, reformatted into this
            package's schema, and redistributed as part of its dataset.
            Counts from this source are NOT used (it reports 775 local
            units against the gazetted 753); only coordinates, postal codes,
            Devanagari names and slugs are consumed, each flagged as
            supplementary. This source is never used as an identifier.

2. Geographical Codes for States, Districts and Local Bodies
   (Open Data Nepal, harvested from the Central Bureau of Statistics)
   Source:  https://opendatanepal.com/dataset/geographical-codes-for-states-districts-and-local-bodies
   License: Creative Commons Attribution (CC-BY),
            https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
            (license_id "cc-by" in the dataset metadata, re-verified at
            acquisition; metadata unchanged since 2026-06-14)
   Used for: the authoritative CBS hierarchical codes — 77 districts
            (101-709), 753 local bodies (10101-70909), 7 states — and
            Devanagari names at palika level where verified aligned.
            As of v2.5.0 also: the official contact block (website, email,
            phone) for local bodies, joined on Devanagari name because the
            harvest carries no identifiers.
   Adaptation: codes are reconciled against two further sources and
            redistributed per-record with nsoCodeVerified flags;
            per-record provenance is recorded in data/SOURCES.md.
            The districts file's Devanagari column (corrupt from row 43
            in the upstream CSV) is never consumed.

